            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous multivessel coronary artery dissection in a young asymptomatic patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>123-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A unique case of spontaneous multivessel coronary artery dissection in a young woman without identifiable risk factors, who remained asymptomatic despite extensive coronary dissection is presented. The management of this condition and a review of the current literature on this subject are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
